WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.970
Lobbying threshold twenty twenty-six.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.602
More lobbying, now registered.

00:00:05.602 --> 00:00:11.306
On January 19, 2026, Canada lowered the lobbying registration threshold.

00:00:11.306 --> 00:00:17.125
Previously, a person had to spend twenty percent of their duties on lobbying to require registration.

00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:22.784
Now, anyone who lobbies for eight hours or more in a consecutive four-week period must register.

00:00:22.784 --> 00:00:26.272
This means more lobbyists will appear in the registry.

00:00:26.272 --> 00:00:29.954
The question is: does registration produce accountability?

00:00:29.954 --> 00:00:33.147
The lobbying registry has always been public.

00:00:33.147 --> 00:00:38.522
Five thousand registered lobbyists file thirteen thousand communication reports annually.

00:00:38.522 --> 00:00:44.034
The regulatory capture documented across this site occurred with full registration and disclosure.

00:00:44.034 --> 00:00:46.477
Registration is visibility.

00:00:46.477 --> 00:00:48.488
It is not enforcement.

00:00:48.488 --> 00:00:53.056
More lobbyists on the registry does not mean fewer captured regulators.

00:00:53.056 --> 00:00:55.102
The threshold change.

00:00:55.102 --> 00:01:03.840
Before January 2026: lobbying registration required if lobbying constituted a significant part of duties, interpreted as twenty percent.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:11.693
After January 2026: registration required if lobbying for eight hours or more in any consecutive four-week period.

00:01:11.693 --> 00:01:16.261
What the threshold change means for lobbying transparency and accountability.

00:01:16.261 --> 00:01:18.749
Visibility without enforcement.

00:01:18.749 --> 00:01:22.590
The lobbying threshold change is a transparency improvement.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.238
But transparency without enforcement is documentation, not accountability.

00:01:27.238 --> 00:01:31.602
The lobbying registry has always documented who meets whom about what.

00:01:31.602 --> 00:01:34.568
It has never prevented captured outcomes.

00:01:34.568 --> 00:01:39.522
More lobbyists on the registry means more data for investigations like TENET5.

00:01:39.522 --> 00:01:44.499
It does not mean fewer captured regulators or more accountable policy outcomes.

00:01:44.499 --> 00:01:46.943
The threshold change is welcome.

00:01:46.943 --> 00:01:54.102
But it does not change the fundamental architecture of institutional capture documented across two hundred and thirty pages on this site.
